From c062635f7b157051089d508fb6e50cc9082d10ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 07:26:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/33] mmc: sunxi: Propagate reset lookup errors

The optional reset getter returns NULL when no reset exists and an error
pointer on lookup failures. Do not treat non-defer failures as absent.

Fixes: 9e71c589e44d ("mmc: sunxi: Use devm_reset_control_get_optional() for reset control")
Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 59636ee3afbe..99acac8fbb48 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1345,8 +1345,9 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_resource_request(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host,
 
 	host->reset = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(&pdev->dev,
 								"ahb");
-	if (PTR_ERR(host->reset) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
-		return PTR_ERR(host->reset);
+	if (IS_ERR(host->reset))
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(host->reset),
+				     "Failed to get reset control\n");
 
 	ret = sunxi_mmc_enable(host);
 	if (ret)
-- 
